insert into public.flashcards (id, cert, deck, domain, objective, front, back) values
('a2-f-036','aplus2','core',1,'1.1',$$What is the key difference between Windows Home and Pro editions?$$,$$Windows Pro adds features Home lacks, including BitLocker drive encryption, the ability to join a domain, and Group Policy management - important for business/enterprise deployment scenarios.$$),
('a2-f-037','aplus2','core',1,'1.2',$$What does the sfc /scannow command do?$$,$$Scans all protected Windows system files and repairs corrupted or modified files by replacing them with cached correct versions - used when core OS files are suspected of being damaged.$$),
('a2-f-038','aplus2','core',1,'1.2',$$What does the chkdsk command do?$$,$$Checks the file system and file system metadata of a disk volume for logical and physical errors, and can repair them - used when disk corruption or bad sectors are suspected.$$),
('a2-f-039','aplus2','core',1,'1.3',$$When would exFAT be preferred over NTFS or FAT32?$$,$$exFAT supports files larger than 4GB (unlike FAT32) and is natively readable/writable across Windows, macOS, and many other devices without needing NTFS drivers - ideal for cross-platform external/USB drives.$$),
('a2-f-040','aplus2','core',1,'1.1',$$What is the difference between Task Manager and Device Manager?$$,$$Task Manager monitors and manages running processes, resource usage (CPU/RAM/disk/network), and startup programs. Device Manager manages hardware devices and their drivers, useful for identifying driver conflicts or failures.$$),
('a2-f-041','aplus2','core',1,'1.4',$$What does macOS Time Machine do?$$,$$Provides built-in, automatic incremental backups to an external or network drive, allowing a user to restore individual files or the entire system to a previous point in time.$$),
('a2-f-042','aplus2','core',1,'1.5',$$What does chmod 755 grant in Linux file permissions?$$,$$Owner: read/write/execute (7); Group: read/execute (5); Others: read/execute (5) - a common permission set for executable scripts that should be run, but not modified, by non-owners.$$),
('a2-f-043','aplus2','core',1,'1.1',$$What is the difference between an in-place upgrade, a clean install, and image deployment?$$,$$An in-place upgrade preserves apps/files/settings while upgrading the OS. A clean install wipes the drive and installs fresh, losing existing data unless backed up. Image deployment applies a pre-configured OS image to (often many) machines at once.$$),
('a2-f-044','aplus2','core',2,'2.1',$$What does BitLocker do?$$,$$Provides full-disk encryption for the Windows OS drive (and optionally other drives), protecting data confidentiality if a device is lost or stolen, since the drive's contents are unreadable without the decryption key.$$),
('a2-f-045','aplus2','core',2,'2.2',$$What is the purpose of User Account Control (UAC)?$$,$$Prompts for confirmation (or admin credentials) before allowing an action that requires elevated privileges, preventing malware or accidental actions from silently making system-level changes.$$),
('a2-f-046','aplus2','core',2,'2.3',$$What is a rootkit?$$,$$Malware that embeds itself at the OS or kernel level, actively hiding its own presence and often other malware, making it especially difficult to detect with standard antivirus tools.$$),
('a2-f-047','aplus2','core',2,'2.3',$$What is a keylogger?$$,$$Malware (or hardware device) that records every keystroke a user types, commonly used to steal usernames, passwords, and other sensitive typed information.$$),
('a2-f-048','aplus2','core',2,'2.4',$$What is the difference between shoulder surfing and tailgating?$$,$$Shoulder surfing is visually observing someone entering sensitive information (like a PIN) without their knowledge. Tailgating is physically following an authorized person through a secured door without independently authenticating.$$),
('a2-f-049','aplus2','core',2,'2.5',$$Why should workstations be configured to auto-lock after a period of inactivity?$$,$$Prevents an unauthorized person from accessing an unattended, still-logged-in workstation - a simple but critical physical/session security control.$$),
('a2-f-050','aplus2','core',2,'2.1',$$Why disable AutoPlay/Autorun for removable media?$$,$$Prevents malicious code on a USB drive or disc from automatically executing the moment the media is inserted, closing off a common malware infection vector.$$),
('a2-f-051','aplus2','core',2,'2.6',$$Why is full-device encryption important on mobile devices before they are ever lost?$$,$$Encryption must be enabled in advance - once a device is lost, it is too late to encrypt it. Pre-emptive encryption ensures data remains protected even if the device falls into the wrong hands.$$),
('a2-f-052','aplus2','core',3,'3.1',$$What are the seven steps of the CompTIA malware removal process, in order?$$,$$1) Investigate and verify malware symptoms. 2) Quarantine infected systems. 3) Disable System Restore (in Windows). 4) Remediate the infected system (update/scan/remove). 5) Schedule scans and run updates. 6) Enable System Restore and create a restore point. 7) Educate the end user.$$),
('a2-f-053','aplus2','core',3,'3.2',$$What is Safe Mode used for in Windows troubleshooting?$$,$$Boots Windows with only a minimal set of essential drivers and services, helping isolate whether a problem is caused by a third-party driver, startup program, or software conflict.$$),
('a2-f-054','aplus2','core',3,'3.1',$$What does System Restore do, and what does it NOT affect?$$,$$Reverts system files, installed programs, and registry settings to an earlier restore point, but does NOT affect personal files (documents, photos, etc.), which remain unchanged.$$),
('a2-f-055','aplus2','core',3,'3.3',$$What should be checked first when an application repeatedly crashes after a Windows update?$$,$$Check for an available application update or known compatibility fix from the vendor - a common cause of post-update crashes is the application not yet supporting a changed OS component.$$),
('a2-f-056','aplus2','core',3,'3.4',$$What should be checked first when a mobile app fails to sync data?$$,$$Verify the account credentials are still valid and that the device has active network connectivity - the two most common root causes of sync failures.$$),
('a2-f-057','aplus2','core',3,'3.5',$$What does a browser certificate warning ("connection not private") indicate?$$,$$The site's TLS certificate is invalid, expired, self-signed, or does not match the domain - potentially indicating a misconfiguration or, in some cases, an active man-in-the-middle attack. Users should not proceed without investigating.$$),
('a2-f-058','aplus2','core',4,'4.1',$$Why is maintaining a knowledge base of past incidents and resolutions valuable?$$,$$Speeds up future troubleshooting by letting technicians reference how similar issues were previously diagnosed and resolved, preserving institutional knowledge beyond any one technician's memory.$$),
('a2-f-059','aplus2','core',4,'4.2',$$Why does change management require a documented rollback plan before implementing a change?$$,$$Ensures the team can quickly and safely revert to the previous known-good state if the change causes unexpected problems, minimizing downtime and impact.$$),
('a2-f-060','aplus2','core',4,'4.3',$$What is the 3-2-1 backup rule?$$,$$Keep 3 total copies of important data, on 2 different types of media, with 1 copy stored offsite - a widely recommended baseline for resilient backup strategy.$$),
('a2-f-061','aplus2','core',4,'4.4',$$Why should a technician use an ESD strap or mat before working inside a PC case?$$,$$Prevents electrostatic discharge from the technician's body from damaging sensitive electronic components, even when the PC is powered off and unplugged.$$),
('a2-f-062','aplus2','core',4,'4.5',$$Why is active listening and avoiding technical jargon important when supporting end users?$$,$$Ensures the technician accurately understands the actual problem (rather than assuming) and that the user can understand and follow any instructions given - both improve resolution speed and user trust.$$),
('a2-f-063','aplus2','core',4,'4.6',$$What is the difference between personal use and corporate/volume licensing for software?$$,$$Personal use licenses typically permit installation on a single device for one individual; corporate/volume licenses permit deployment across many machines under a single agreement, often with centralized management and different usage terms.$$);
insert into public.questions (id, cert, domain, objective, qtype, difficulty, stem, choices, answer, explanation) values
('a2-q-041','aplus2',1,'1.1','mcq',2,$q$A company needs to join workstations to a Windows domain and enforce Group Policy. Which minimum Windows edition supports this?$q$,$q$["Windows Pro","Windows Home","Windows Starter","Any edition supports domain join"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Windows Pro (and higher editions) adds domain join and Group Policy management, which Windows Home lacks entirely.$q$),
('a2-q-042','aplus2',1,'1.2','mcq',2,$q$A user suspects that critical Windows system files have become corrupted after a failed update. Which command should a technician run to scan for and repair them?$q$,$q$["sfc /scannow","chkdsk /f","diskpart","ipconfig /flushdns"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$sfc /scannow specifically scans protected system files and repairs corrupted ones using cached correct copies.$q$),
('a2-q-043','aplus2',1,'1.2','mcq',2,$q$A drive is suspected of having file system corruption or bad sectors after several unexpected shutdowns. Which command should be used to check and repair it?$q$,$q$["chkdsk","sfc /scannow","tracert","netstat"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$chkdsk specifically checks a volume's file system and metadata for errors and can repair logical and some physical disk issues.$q$),
('a2-q-044','aplus2',1,'1.3','mcq',2,$q$A user needs to format a USB drive so it can store individual files larger than 4GB and remain readable on both Windows and macOS without installing extra drivers. Which file system should they choose?$q$,$q$["exFAT","FAT32","NTFS","ext4"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$exFAT supports files over 4GB (unlike FAT32) and is natively compatible across Windows and macOS, unlike NTFS which requires additional drivers for full macOS write support.$q$),
('a2-q-045','aplus2',1,'1.1','mcq',2,$q$A technician needs to identify which running process is consuming excessive CPU and end it. Which built-in Windows tool should they use?$q$,$q$["Task Manager","Device Manager","Disk Management","Control Panel"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Task Manager displays running processes and their resource usage, and lets a technician end a misbehaving process directly.$q$),
('a2-q-046','aplus2',1,'1.1','mcq',2,$q$A newly installed printer is not working, and the technician suspects a driver conflict. Which tool should they check first?$q$,$q$["Device Manager","Task Manager","File Explorer","Windows Update history only"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Device Manager shows installed hardware and driver status, including conflict indicators (like a yellow warning icon), making it the correct tool for diagnosing driver issues.$q$),
('a2-q-047','aplus2',1,'1.4','mcq',2,$q$A Mac user wants to restore a single deleted file from three days ago without affecting anything else on the system. Which built-in feature should they use?$q$,$q$["Time Machine","Finder alone","Keychain Access","Disk Utility"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Time Machine maintains automatic incremental backups, allowing a user to browse and restore individual files from any past backup point.$q$),
('a2-q-048','aplus2',1,'1.5','mcq',2,$q$A Linux administrator runs chmod 755 on a shell script. What permissions does this grant?$q$,$q$["Owner: read/write/execute; Group: read/execute; Others: read/execute","Owner: read only; Group: write only; Others: execute only","Full permissions for everyone including write access","No permissions for anyone"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$755 in chmod numeric notation grants the owner full read/write/execute (7), while group and others receive read/execute only (5), a common setting for shared executable scripts.$q$),
('a2-q-049','aplus2',1,'1.1','mcq',2,$q$A technician needs to upgrade a user's Windows 10 PC to Windows 11 while preserving all installed applications, files, and settings. What type of installation should they perform?$q$,$q$["An in-place upgrade","A clean install","Image deployment to a new machine","A repair install using a Linux live USB"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$An in-place upgrade preserves existing applications, files, and settings while upgrading the OS version, unlike a clean install which wipes the drive.$q$),
('a2-q-050','aplus2',2,'2.1','mcq',2,$q$A company wants to ensure that if a laptop is lost or stolen, its entire drive contents remain unreadable without the correct key. Which Windows feature should be enabled?$q$,$q$["BitLocker","Windows Defender Firewall","UAC","Task Scheduler"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$BitLocker provides full-disk encryption for the OS drive, ensuring the data remains protected and unreadable if the physical device is lost or stolen.$q$),
('a2-q-051','aplus2',2,'2.2','mcq',2,$q$A user installing new software is prompted with a dialog asking them to confirm the action before it proceeds with elevated privileges. What Windows feature caused this prompt?$q$,$q$["User Account Control (UAC)","Windows Defender Firewall","BitLocker","Task Manager"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$UAC prompts for confirmation or admin credentials before allowing privileged actions, preventing malware or accidental changes from silently making system-level modifications.$q$),
('a2-q-052','aplus2',2,'2.3','mcq',3,$q$A PC exhibits strange behavior, but standard antivirus scans repeatedly report no infection, even though system performance and behavior strongly suggest malware. What type of malware is most consistent with this scenario?$q$,$q$["A rootkit","A simple adware pop-up generator","A macro virus in a document","A basic phishing email"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Rootkits specifically embed themselves at the OS/kernel level and actively conceal their own presence, which is why standard antivirus scans often fail to detect them despite clear behavioral symptoms.$q$),
('a2-q-053','aplus2',2,'2.3','mcq',2,$q$Several employees report that their banking passwords were used fraudulently shortly after typing them on a shared, unmonitored kiosk PC. What type of malware most likely caused this?$q$,$q$["A keylogger","A boot sector virus","A worm","Ransomware"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$A keylogger records every keystroke typed, which is exactly the mechanism that would allow an attacker to capture passwords typed on a compromised shared PC.$q$),
('a2-q-054','aplus2',2,'2.4','mcq',2,$q$A coworker watches an employee enter their PIN at a badge-secured door without the employee's knowledge, then later uses the observed PIN to gain unauthorized entry. What social engineering technique was used to obtain the PIN?$q$,$q$["Shoulder surfing","Tailgating","Phishing","Whaling"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Shoulder surfing is visually observing someone entering sensitive information without their knowledge - exactly how the PIN was obtained here.$q$),
('a2-q-055','aplus2',2,'2.4','mcq',2,$q$An unauthorized person follows closely behind an employee through a secured door as it closes, without badging in themselves. What social engineering technique is this?$q$,$q$["Tailgating","Shoulder surfing","Vishing","Pretexting"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Tailgating is physically following an authorized person through a secured entry point without independently authenticating - a purely physical social engineering technique.$q$),
('a2-q-056','aplus2',2,'2.5','mcq',2,$q$Why should office workstations be configured to automatically lock after 5-10 minutes of inactivity?$q$,$q$["It prevents unauthorized access to an unattended workstation that remains logged in","It saves significantly more power than sleep mode","It automatically updates the operating system","It disables the need for any password at all"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Auto-lock closes the window of opportunity for someone to walk up to an unattended, still-logged-in workstation and access it without any credentials.$q$),
('a2-q-057','aplus2',2,'2.1','mcq',2,$q$A technician disables AutoPlay/Autorun for removable media across the organization's PCs. What risk does this specifically reduce?$q$,$q$["Malicious code on a USB drive automatically executing the moment it is inserted","The PC's boot time increasing","Users being unable to open any USB drive at all","Wireless network interference"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$AutoPlay/Autorun can automatically execute code from removable media upon insertion; disabling it closes off this common malware infection vector.$q$),
('a2-q-058','aplus2',2,'2.6','mcq',2,$q$A company wants to ensure that if any employee's phone is lost in the future, its data remains protected. When should full-device encryption be enabled to be effective?$q$,$q$["Before the device is ever lost - encryption cannot be applied retroactively after the fact","Only after the device is reported lost","Only if the device contains no sensitive data","Encryption is unnecessary for mobile devices"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Encryption must already be active for it to protect data on a device that is later lost - it provides no benefit if enabled only after the loss has occurred.$q$),
('a2-q-059','aplus2',2,'2.3','mcq',2,$q$An employee receives an email that appears to be from their bank, urging them to click a link and enter their login credentials on a page that closely mimics the real bank site. What type of attack is this?$q$,$q$["Phishing","A rootkit infection","A keylogger installation","Tailgating"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Phishing uses a deceptive message impersonating a trusted entity to trick the victim into revealing credentials or other sensitive information on a fraudulent page.$q$),
('a2-q-060','aplus2',3,'3.1','mcq',3,$q$Which sequence correctly follows the CompTIA seven-step malware removal process?$q$,$q$["Investigate and verify, quarantine, disable System Restore, remediate, schedule scans/updates, enable System Restore, educate the user","Remediate, quarantine, investigate, educate the user, disable System Restore, enable System Restore, schedule scans","Educate the user, quarantine, remediate, investigate, disable System Restore, enable System Restore, schedule scans","Quarantine, remediate, educate the user, investigate, enable System Restore, disable System Restore, schedule scans"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$The correct order is: investigate/verify symptoms, quarantine the infected system, disable System Restore, remediate (update/scan/remove), schedule ongoing scans/updates, re-enable System Restore, then educate the end user.$q$),
('a2-q-061','aplus2',3,'3.1','mcq',3,$q$Why does the CompTIA malware removal process call for disabling System Restore before remediating an infection?$q$,$q$["To prevent the malware from being preserved in a restore point and later reintroduced if the system is ever rolled back","System Restore has no relevance to malware removal","Disabling System Restore speeds up the antivirus scan itself","It is required to enable Safe Mode"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$If System Restore remains active during an infection, a restore point could capture the malware itself, allowing it to be reintroduced later via a rollback - disabling it first prevents this.$q$),
('a2-q-062','aplus2',3,'3.2','mcq',2,$q$A technician boots a malfunctioning Windows PC using only a minimal set of essential drivers and services to determine whether a third-party driver is causing the problem. What is this boot mode called?$q$,$q$["Safe Mode","Recovery Mode only","BIOS setup mode","Sleep mode"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Safe Mode loads only essential drivers and services, helping isolate whether a problem originates from a third-party driver or startup program versus core Windows components.$q$),
('a2-q-063','aplus2',3,'3.1','mcq',2,$q$A user's PC is reverted to a restore point from last week to fix a software conflict. What happens to the user's personal documents created since that restore point?$q$,$q$["They remain unchanged, since System Restore does not affect personal files","They are permanently deleted","They are also reverted to their state from last week","They are automatically backed up to OneDrive"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$System Restore only reverts system files, installed programs, and registry settings - personal files like documents and photos are explicitly unaffected.$q$),
('a2-q-064','aplus2',3,'3.3','mcq',2,$q$An application consistently crashes immediately after a recent Windows feature update, though it worked fine before. What should a technician check first?$q$,$q$["Whether an application update or vendor compatibility fix is available for the new Windows version","Whether the power supply is failing","Whether the monitor cable is loose","Whether the case fans need cleaning"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Post-update application crashes commonly result from the application not yet supporting a changed OS component - checking for a vendor update or compatibility fix directly addresses this likely cause.$q$),
('a2-q-065','aplus2',3,'3.4','mcq',2,$q$A mobile banking app suddenly fails to sync recent transactions. What should be checked first?$q$,$q$["That the account credentials are still valid and the device has active network connectivity","That the phone's screen brightness is set correctly","That the phone case is properly attached","That the phone's ringtone volume is turned up"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Invalid/expired credentials and lost network connectivity are the two most common root causes of a mobile app sync failure, making them the logical first checks.$q$),
('a2-q-066','aplus2',3,'3.5','mcq',2,$q$A user's browser displays "Your connection is not private" when visiting a familiar company website. What should the user do?$q$,$q$["Avoid proceeding until the certificate issue is investigated, since it could indicate a misconfiguration or a man-in-the-middle attack","Always click through the warning immediately without concern","Assume the website has permanently shut down","Disable their antivirus software to fix the warning"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$A certificate warning can indicate an expired, misconfigured, or fraudulent certificate - potentially a man-in-the-middle attack - so it should be investigated rather than dismissed automatically.$q$),
('a2-q-067','aplus2',3,'3.1','mcq',3,$q$A PC restarts unexpectedly at random times with no error message displayed to the user. Where should a technician look first to identify a possible cause?$q$,$q$["The Windows Event Viewer logs","The printer queue","The wallpaper settings","The Recycle Bin"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Event Viewer records system, application, and security events including crash and restart causes, making it the correct first place to investigate an unexplained random restart.$q$),
('a2-q-068','aplus2',3,'3.1','mcq',2,$q$Antivirus software quarantines a file that a user insists is a legitimate, needed application component. What is the appropriate next step?$q$,$q$["Verify whether the detection is a false positive before deciding to restore the file or leave it quarantined","Immediately restore the file without any verification","Permanently delete the entire application folder","Disable the antivirus software going forward"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Quarantined files should be verified (e.g., checked against the vendor, scanned with a second tool) before being restored, since assuming either "safe" or "malicious" without verification risks either data loss or reinfection.$q$),
('a2-q-069','aplus2',3,'3.1','mcq',2,$q$A PC that has been in daily use for two years has become noticeably slower, though a malware scan finds no infection. What is a common, non-malware cause of this symptom?$q$,$q$["Too many startup programs and insufficient free disk space accumulated over time","A failing power supply, always","A newly installed CPU","A corrupted BIOS"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Gradual slowdown over long-term use is commonly caused by accumulated startup programs consuming resources at boot and low free disk space, rather than a hardware failure or malware.$q$),
('a2-q-070','aplus2',4,'4.1','mcq',2,$q$A support team maintains a searchable record of past incidents and how each was resolved. What is the primary benefit of this practice?$q$,$q$["It speeds up future troubleshooting by preserving institutional knowledge beyond any single technician's memory","It replaces the need for any technician training","It automatically resolves all future tickets without human involvement","It eliminates the need for a ticketing system"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$A knowledge base lets any technician reference how similar past issues were diagnosed and resolved, speeding up resolution and reducing reliance on any one person's memory.$q$),
('a2-q-071','aplus2',4,'4.2','mcq',2,$q$Before implementing a change to a production system, the change management process requires a documented rollback plan. Why?$q$,$q$["To allow the team to quickly and safely revert to the previous known-good state if the change causes unexpected problems","Rollback plans are only required for cosmetic changes","It replaces the need for testing the change beforehand","It is only a formality with no practical purpose"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$A rollback plan minimizes downtime and impact by ensuring a fast, safe path back to the previous working state if a change does not go as expected.$q$),
('a2-q-072','aplus2',4,'4.3','mcq',2,$q$A company wants a resilient backup strategy that protects against both hardware failure and a site-wide disaster like a fire. Which backup approach follows the widely recommended 3-2-1 rule?$q$,$q$["3 total copies of the data, on 2 different media types, with 1 copy stored offsite","1 copy of the data stored locally only","3 copies of the data all stored on the same external drive","2 copies of the data, both stored in the same building"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$The 3-2-1 rule specifically requires an offsite copy to survive a site-wide disaster, plus media diversity to protect against a single media type's failure mode.$q$),
('a2-q-073','aplus2',4,'4.4','mcq',2,$q$Before replacing a component inside a desktop's case, a technician puts on a wrist strap connected to a grounding point. What risk does this address?$q$,$q$["Electrostatic discharge (ESD) damaging sensitive components","Electrical shock from a fully unplugged PC","Dust inhalation","Repetitive strain injury"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Even with the PC unplugged, static discharge from the technician's body can permanently damage sensitive electronic components - an ESD strap grounds the technician to prevent this.$q$),
('a2-q-074','aplus2',4,'4.5','mcq',2,$q$A technician explains a fix to a non-technical user using plain language instead of technical jargon, and confirms understanding before ending the call. What professional skill does this demonstrate?$q$,$q$["Effective communication tailored to the audience","Avoiding all documentation requirements","Bypassing standard troubleshooting steps","Escalating unnecessarily"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Communicating clearly and appropriately for the audience improves user understanding, satisfaction, and the likelihood that any follow-up instructions are correctly followed.$q$),
('a2-q-075','aplus2',4,'4.6','mcq',2,$q$Before disposing of a used printer toner cartridge, what should a technician consult?$q$,$q$["The Safety Data Sheet (SDS) and local environmental disposal regulations","The printer's video output settings","The Wi-Fi password documentation","The warranty registration card only"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Toner and other consumables often require special handling and disposal per environmental regulations, detailed in the product's Safety Data Sheet.$q$),
('a2-q-076','aplus2',4,'4.6','mcq',2,$q$A business purchases a volume license agreement to deploy the same software across 200 workstations under a single centrally managed agreement. How does this differ from a personal use license?$q$,$q$["A volume/corporate license permits deployment across many machines under one agreement, often with centralized management, unlike a personal use license limited to a single device/individual","There is no difference between personal and volume licensing","A personal use license always covers unlimited installations","Volume licenses are always free of charge"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Volume/corporate licensing is specifically designed for deploying software across many machines under one agreement, while personal use licenses are typically restricted to a single device or individual.$q$),
('a2-q-077','aplus2',4,'4.5','mcq',2,$q$A user describes a vague problem, and a technician resists the urge to immediately assume the cause, instead asking clarifying questions and letting the user finish explaining. What benefit does this behavior provide?$q$,$q$["It ensures accurate problem identification and avoids wasted effort troubleshooting the wrong issue","It guarantees the fastest possible ticket closure regardless of accuracy","It eliminates the need for any further troubleshooting steps","It has no effect on the outcome of the ticket"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Actively listening rather than assuming ensures the technician addresses the actual problem, avoiding wasted time chasing an incorrect assumption about the cause.$q$),
('a2-q-078','aplus2',4,'4.2','mcq',2,$q$A company requires every proposed change to a production system to go through a documented request, review, and approval process before implementation. What is this process called?$q$,$q$["Change management","Asset management","Incident management exclusively","Knowledge management"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Change management is the structured process governing how changes to production systems are requested, reviewed, approved, and implemented in a controlled way.$q$),
('a2-q-079','aplus2',4,'4.4','mcq',2,$q$Which of the following is a recommended physical safety practice when lifting a heavy piece of equipment like a server or large monitor?$q$,$q$["Lift with the legs, keeping the back straight, rather than bending at the waist","Always lift alone regardless of weight to save time","Twist the torso while lifting to reposition the item faster","Hold the item as far from the body as possible while lifting"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Proper lifting technique (bending at the knees, keeping the back straight, and lifting with the legs) reduces the risk of back injury when handling heavy equipment.$q$),
('a2-q-080','aplus2',4,'4.1','mcq',2,$q$Why is it important to keep network diagrams and asset documentation up to date?$q$,$q$["It speeds up troubleshooting and supports accurate planning when implementing future changes","It is only useful for regulatory audits and has no operational value","It replaces the need for a help desk ticketing system","Outdated documentation carries no risk as long as the network still works"]$q$::jsonb,'0'::jsonb,$q$Accurate, current documentation helps technicians quickly understand the environment during troubleshooting and helps teams plan changes without unexpected surprises from undocumented systems.$q$);
